---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { GITHUB_URL } from '../config';

const crates = [
  ['motion-core', 'The scene: layers, transforms, colours, geometry and ids (no interface).'],
  ['motion-animation', 'Animations, easing, presets, and working out the scene at any time.'],
  ['motion-timeline', 'Time to pixels on the timeline, snapping, dragging and resizing bars.'],
  ['motion-render', 'Drawing with Vello on the GPU: shapes, text, images, effects.'],
  ['motion-project', 'The project format, saving, media, undo and redo, crash recovery, mockups.'],
  ['motion-export', 'Export: frame timing, PNG, FFmpeg video and GIF, Lottie, sound mixing.'],
  ['motion-ui', 'The editor: canvas, timeline, layers, inspector and commands.'],
  ['motion-app', 'The emaki program: window, menus, dialogs, Home, export jobs, autosave, command line.'],
  ['motion-figma', 'Turning Figma frames into Emaki layers.'],
  ['motion-library', 'Brand kits, saved elements and the bundled icons.'],
  ['motion-track', 'Point tracking in video, for pinning layers to moving things.'],
];
---

<Page
  title="Contributing"
  description="How to build Emaki from source, how the code is laid out, and how to propose changes once the code is public."
  heading="Help make Emaki great"
>
  <p slot="intro">
    {
      GITHUB_URL ? (
        <>
          Bug reports, ideas and pull requests are all welcome. The code is on <a href={GITHUB_URL}>GitHub</a>.
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          The code isn't public yet. Once it is, bug reports, ideas and pull requests are all welcome, and this page
          is how it will work.
        </>
      )
    }
  </p>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Build it from source</h2>
    <p>
      You need Rust stable 1.95 or newer and a graphics card with Vulkan (Metal on macOS, DirectX 12 on Windows). On
      Linux, also the ALSA development files (<code>libasound2-dev</code> or similar) for sound, and FFmpeg on your
      <code>PATH</code> for video export.
    </p>
    <pre><code>cargo run --release -p motion-app -- examples/demo.emaki</code></pre>
    <p>Before you send a change, run the same checks as the project: formatting, Clippy with warnings as errors, and every test.</p>
    <pre><code>scripts/verify.sh</code></pre>

    <h2>How the code is laid out</h2>
    <p>A Rust workspace of small crates, from the scene model up to the app:</p>
  </div>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th scope="col">Crate</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {
          crates.map(([name, what]) => (
            <tr>
              <td><code>{name}</code></td>
              <td>{what}</td>
            </tr>
          ))
        }
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>There's also <code>figma-plugin/</code> (the Figma plugin, in TypeScript) and <code>docs/</code>.</p>

    <h2>Proposing a change</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Big changes start as an issue</strong>, so we can agree on the approach before you spend time on it.</li>
      <li><strong>One change per pull request</strong>, with tests. Test names are sentences, such as <code>a_mockup_plays_with_the_artboard_it_shows</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Interface changes come with light-mode screenshots</strong>, before and after, from the screenshot tests.</li>
      <li>Small fixes to copy and docs are welcome too.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Interface and copy</h2>
    <p>The interface follows the project's UI guidelines (<code>docs/design/ui-guidelines.md</code>). In brief:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Colours, sizes and spacing come from the theme's tokens, and controls from the shared widget helpers.</li>
      <li>24 px rows, 8 px gaps and a 12 px inset; type at 11, 12, 13 or 16 px only.</li>
      <li>Lucide icons, each with a hit area of at least 24 px and a tooltip.</li>
      <li>Copy in British English and sentence case, in plain, direct sentences. Errors start with “Couldn’t…”.</li>
      <li>No other apps’ names in the interface.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Code of conduct</h2>
    <p>
      Be kind and assume good intent. Emaki follows the
      <a href="https://www.contributor-covenant.org/version/2/1/code_of_conduct/">Contributor Covenant</a>: harassment
      or personal attacks of any kind aren't welcome, and the maintainer may remove comments or contributors that
      break it.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      Please don't report security problems in public issues. Once the code is public, report them privately through
      the repository's GitHub security advisories
      {GITHUB_URL ? <a href={`${GITHUB_URL}/security/advisories/new`}>(report a vulnerability)</a> : ''}.
    </p>
  </div>
</Page>
